// Title: Suspicious Rundll32 Activity Invoking Sys File
// Sigma ID: 731231b9-0b5d-4219-94dd-abb6959aa7ea
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-03-05 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011
// Description: Detects suspicious process related to rundll32 based on command line that includes a *.sys file
//   as seen being used by UNC2452
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/04/goldmax-goldfinder-sibot-analyzing-nobelium-malware/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_sys.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "rundll32.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains ".sys," or ProcessCommandLine contains ".sys ")
